OL,3,GNEWSA'Punjabi Sky Blues celebrates
OL,4,Afootball and heritage'
OL,5,
OL,6,FGrowing up, Parmdip Dhillon was one of
OL,7,Fthe only Coventry City fans in his
OL,8,Ffriendship group.
OL,10,FMany of the people he knew supported
OL,11,Fthe "bigger", more popular clubs,
OL,12,Frather than their home team.
OL,14,FPart of a Punjabi family, he watched as
OL,15,Fhis relatives - who also loved football
OL,16,F- joined supporters groups in their own
OL,17,Fclubs, like Punjabi Wolves.
OL,19,F"I saw that group flourishing, and I
OL,20,Fthought: 'Why don't we have our own in
OL,21,FCoventry for Coventry City?'" he said.
